<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  THIS FILE IS WHY THE HEADER BADGE AND THE TOAST UPDATE IN REAL TIME
  ===========================================================================
  Magento_Customer/js/customer-data listens on `ajaxComplete`, asks
  section-config which sections the request's URL affects, and re-fetches just
  those. So the two things that have to change after a heart is pressed are
  declared here rather than pushed by hand from the toggle's own JavaScript:

    wishlist   carries `count` (Plugin/CustomerData/AddNumericCount) and
               `product_ids` (Plugin/CustomerData/AddProductIds). Re-fetching
               it updates the header's numeral AND repaints every heart on the
               page from one source of truth - including the SECOND card for
               the same product, which a hand-rolled DOM update would miss.

    messages   Magento\Theme\CustomerData\Messages drains the session's
               messages and hands them to Magento_Theme/js/view/messages,
               which is what renders them into `.page.messages` - the toast.
               Declared EXPLICITLY and not left to core: the message cookie
               path (Magento\Theme\Controller\Result\MessagePlugin) bails out
               on `instanceof Json`, so a JSON response carries no messages of
               its own and this section is the only route a toast has after an
               AJAX POST.

  Nothing about either is invented for this feature - it is Magento's own
  private-content pipeline, which is also why none of it can be full-page
  cached by mistake.

  ===========================================================================
  THE ACTION NAME IS THE frontName, NOT THE ROUTE ID
  ===========================================================================
  This said `spartrak_wishlist/ajax/toggle` - with an UNDERSCORE - and that one
  character is why the header badge never updated in real time. It was reported
  as "the counter does not change until I remove an item", and the reason the
  toast worked while the numeral did not is right here.

  Magento matches these names against the request's URL PATH, and the path is
  built from the frontName. etc/frontend/routes.xml declares

      <route id="spartrak_wishlist" frontName="spartrak-wishlist">

  so the id and the path differ, and the URL the toggle actually posts to is
  .../ar/spartrak-wishlist/ajax/toggle/. Section-config never matched it.

  MEASURED on the live storefront, through Magento's own resolver:

      getAffectedSections('.../ar/spartrak-wishlist/ajax/toggle/')
          -> ['messages']                 the URL that is really requested
      getAffectedSections('.../ar/spartrak_wishlist/ajax/toggle/')
          -> ['wishlist', 'messages']     the URL nothing ever requests

  `messages` still came back for the real URL because it is configured for
  every action, which is exactly what made this hard to see: the toast appeared
  on every press, so the private-content pipeline looked like it was working.
  Only the section unique to this action was being dropped.

  Core never trips over this because every Magento_Wishlist route has a
  frontName identical to its id (`wishlist/index/add` and so on), so the
  distinction is invisible there and easy to carry over wrongly.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Customer:etc/sections.xsd">
    <action name="spartrak-wishlist/ajax/toggle">
        <section name="wishlist"/>
        <section name="messages"/>
    </action>
</config>
